@startuml
title The five incoming call types — each mapped: source, route, proof, terminal

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af
left to right direction

package "Sources" #fdfdfd {
  [Another tool] as S1
  [A third party\n(their initiative)] as S2
  [A static page\nwe own] as S3
  [Our client\n(has a session)] as S4
  [A tool we\ndispatched] as S5
}

package "Route + proof (declared in the registry)" #fbfdfd {
  [tool_to_tool\nproof: none (internal)\nrelayed, never at the Gate] as R1
  [third_party_callback\nproof: api_key · vault credential\n(mTLS at the infra migration)] as R2
  [static_witness\nproof: none · onload · log only] as R3
  [client_sessioned\nproof: signed session token · per-hop nonce] as R4
  [internal_callback\nproof: our_signature · signed out, verified back] as R5
}

package "Terminal" #fdfdfd {
  [The UniversalNavigatorProxy\n(satellite) or the navigator] as T1
  [The Gate (transport only)\n-> the UniversalNavigator\n(proves every arrival)] as TG
}

S1 --> R1
S2 --> R2
S3 --> R3
S4 --> R4
S5 --> R5

R1 --> T1 : never touches the Gate
R2 --> TG
R3 --> TG
R4 --> TG
R5 --> TG

note bottom of TG
  The Gate is the single client entrance and verifies nothing:
  it collects the session token, HTTP head and parameters and
  passes them to the UniversalNavigator — the only node that
  accepts external traffic. The navigator matches the route in
  the live registry and verifies the proof the route names:
  verify or refuse. An arrival on an unmapped route is refused.
  Only tool_to_tool stays internal, relayed via the
  UniversalNavigatorProxy, never reaching the Gate.
end note
@enduml
